# Studio Answer Key Conventions

## 1. Automatic solution pages

Every template with `producesAnswerKey: true` **automatically** inserts a solution page after the puzzle when generated. There is **no** form toggle (`includeAnswerKey` / `answerKeyForAll` are removed).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — flag only; generate always adds the solution page
producesAnswerKey: true
```

Do **not** add answer-key toggles to `configSchema`. `runStudioGenerateOnce` keys off `producesAnswerKey` alone.

DEV assert in `studio-templates.ts` throws if a template still exposes those field keys.

## 2. Answer-key ink — print-safe monochrome

Answer-key pages tint revealed `studioRole: 'answer'` objects with `answerInk`. Blue (`STUDIO_ANSWER_INK = #1D4ED8`) is for color UI templates only.

For **black-and-white / print-first** worksheets (attention drills, dual-task, stroop, counting, trails, etc.), answer-key ink must be **black**:

- Use `STUDIO_ANSWER_INK_MONO` (`STUDIO_INK` / `#000000`)
- Register the template key in `STUDIO_ANSWER_INK_MONO_TEMPLATES` in `studio.constants.ts`
- `answerInkForTemplate` in `run-studio-generate.ts` reads that set — do not hardcode a new `===` chain

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — B&W sheet gets blue answers on the key page
buildAnswerPage(objects, STUDIO_ANSWER_INK)

// ✅ GOOD — print-safe black
buildAnswerPage(objects, STUDIO_ANSWER_INK_MONO)
// + add template key to STUDIO_ANSWER_INK_MONO_TEMPLATES
```

Only templates that intentionally use color in the puzzle may keep default `STUDIO_ANSWER_INK`.

## Checklist (new `producesAnswerKey` template)

- [ ] `producesAnswerKey: true` (generate auto-adds solution page)
- [ ] Hidden `studioRole: 'answer'` objects on the puzzle page
- [ ] Puzzle fills/strokes monochrome when the sheet is B&W
- [ ] B&W templates listed in `STUDIO_ANSWER_INK_MONO_TEMPLATES`
- [ ] Tests: answer harvest + (if B&W) black ink on answer page
